cco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — فانيليا, بندق, amaretto. The festive range for المتحمسون who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Café Crème';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The Camacho family grew corojo tobacco in Cuba\'s Vuelta Abajo region for generations — not any tobacco, but specifically the corojo varietal whose leaves provide the wrappers that gave Havana\'s great cigars their visual and aromatic signature. Dark, oily, consistently textured, Cuban corojo wrapper was the standard against which every other wrapper tobacco was measured. Growing it was a specialized craft, and the Camachos were among its most accomplished practitioners.\r\n\r\nThe Cuban revolution ended that chapter in 1959. Simon Camacho\'s departure from Havana was the departure of a man carrying his professional identity in seed form — literally, in the case of the corojo plants whose genetics he transported first to Miami and eventually to Honduras. The Jamastran Valley in Honduras\' Olancho Department proved to be the most promising available site: volcanic soils, altitude, and humidity patterns that experienced tobacologists recognized as potentially capable of supporting corojo cultivation.\r\n\r\nThe Honduras corojo that the Camacho family developed over the following decades is not the same plant as Cuban corojo. The terroir is genuinely different — the soil composition, the water, the microbial environment of the fermentation rooms. What resulted was a varietal that shared the visual characteristics and structural quality of the Cuban original while developing its own aromatic profile: fuller-bodied, more pepper-dominant, with an earthiness that Honduran soil imparted rather than Cuban. Several serious tasters have described it as a more extreme version of the Cuban original rather than an approximation.\r\n\r\nThe Davidoff group\'s acquisition in 2008 provided the manufacturing and distribution resources that allowed Camacho\'s transition from specialist manufacturer to international brand. The repositioning around the \'Cigars Gone Loud\' identity was commercially calculated but not inaccurate — Camacho occupies a specific register of intensity and directness that no other major brand in the Davidoff portfolio addresses. The packaging design, the range names, the overall aesthetic of deliberate aggression describe the cigars honestly: these are not subtlety exercises.', `history_es` = 'La familia Camacho cultivaba tabaco corojo en la región cubana de Vuelta Abajo. Tras la revolución, Simon Camacho transportó sus semillas de corojo a Honduras, donde las condiciones climáticas del Valle de Jamastran más se asemejaban a su terroir natal. Este trasplante creó el \'Corojo Hondureño\' — poderoso y complejo. Adquirida por Davidoff en 2008.', `history_de` = 'Die Familie Camacho baute Corojo-Tabak in Kubas Vuelta-Abajo-Region an. Nach der Revolution transportierte Simon Camacho seine Corojo-Samen nach Honduras, wo die klimatischen Bedingungen des Jamastran-Tals seinem Heimatterroir am nächsten kamen. Dieser Verpflanzung schuf den \'Honduranischen Corojo\' — kraftvoll und komplex. 2008 von Davidoff übernommen.', `history_zh` = '卡马乔家族在古巴布埃尔塔阿巴霍地区种植科罗霍烟草。革命后，西蒙·卡马乔将科罗霍种子带到洪都拉斯，那里哈马斯特兰谷的气候条件最接近他的故乡风土。这次移植创造了\'洪都拉斯科罗霍\'——强劲而复杂。2008年被大卫杜夫收购。', `history_ar` = 'زرعت عائلة كاماتشو تبغ الكوروخو في منطقة فويلتا أباخو الكوبية. بعد الثورة، نقل سيمون كاماتشو بذور الكوروخو إلى هندوراس حيث الظروف المناخية لوادي خاماستران أقرب ما تكون لتربته الأصلية. هذا الزرع خلق \'الكوروخو الهندوراسي\' — القوي والمعقد. استُحوِذ عليها ديفيدوف عام 2008.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Notes of red pepper, strong coffee, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Notes of burned coffee, pure cocoa, black licorice. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Notes of bourbon, toasted oak vanilla, soft spices. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Notas de red pimienta, strong café, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Notas de burned café, pure cocoa, black regaliz. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Notas de bourbon, tostado oak vainilla, soft especias. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Noten von red Pfeffer, strong Kaffee, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Noten von burned Kaffee, pure cocoa, black licorice. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Noten von bourbon, geröstet oak Vanille, soft Gewürze. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran 