me\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. نكهات:  burned قهوة, pure cocoa, black عرق السوس. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. نكهات:  bourbon, محمَّص oak فانيليا, soft توابل. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee notes of the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cerveza\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee notas de the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bier\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee Noten von the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"波旁威士忌\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"啤酒\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee 风味： the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"البوربون\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"البيرة\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee نكهات: the Camacho Corojo.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Camacho';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The CAO story begins with pipes, not cigars. Cano Ozgener, who had emigrated from Turkey to Nashville in the 1960s, founded his business in 1968 as a specialist importer of Turkish briars and Meerschaum pipes — products that his cultural background gave him access to through relationships that American competitors could not replicate. Nashville was an unlikely location for a premium tobacco business, but Ozgener understood that his customer base was not geographic but demographic: the serious pipe collector existed in every American city, and direct mail could reach them without a street-level presence.\r\n\r\nThe transition to cigars in the 1990s was both opportunistic and philosophically motivated. The American cigar boom of that decade was creating demand that the established manufacturers were struggling to meet, and Ozgener recognized in cigar culture the same connoisseurship that he had spent twenty years serving in the pipe market. The customer who had spent years developing their taste in briars was exactly the customer who would appreciate serious cigars, and Ozgener had twenty years of relationship with them.\r\n\r\nCAO\'s early cigar identity was deliberately different from the established houses. Where Arturo Fuente communicated heritage and family continuity, and Davidoff communicated Swiss precision and Cuban ancestry, CAO communicated innovation and cultural reference. The Flathead range, named for and designed around the aesthetic of vintage Harley-Davidson V-twin engines, was the most explicit statement of this identity: a premium cigar that addressed the American enthusiast\'s world directly rather than translating European luxury conventions into tobacco form. The Nicaraguan-Honduran blend inside was serious. The packaging and marketing spoke a language the established Havana-influenced houses would not have recognized.\r\n\r\nGeneral Cigar acquired CAO in 2007, bringing the brand\'s innovative character into a portfolio that needed what Macanudo\'s reliable commercial dominance could not provide. The acquisition has maintained CAO\'s identity as the group\'s risk-taking brand — the release schedule that enthusiasts follow for novelty while they rely on Macanudo for consistency.', `history_es` = 'CAO — las iniciales de Cano Ozgener, fundador turco-americano — nació en Nashville en 1968 como importador de pipas turcas. Evolucionó hacia la fabricación de cigarros en los 90. La Flathead (inspirada en motores Harley V-twin), la Pilon (100% nicaragüense) y la Cameroon son sus gammas más emblemáticas. Adquirida por General Cigar en 2007.', `history_de` = 'CAO — die Initialen von Cano Ozgener, dem türkisch-amerikanischen Gründer — wurde 1968 in Nashville als türkischer Pfeifenimporteur geboren. In den 1990ern entwickelte sie sich zur Zigarrenmanufaktur. Die Flathead (inspiriert von Harley V-Twin-Motoren), die Pilon (100% nicaraguanisch) und die Cameroon sind ihre ikonischsten Serien. 2007 von General Cigar übernommen.', `history_zh` = 'CAO——土裔美国创始人卡诺·奥兹格纳的姓名首字母——1968年在纳什维尔以进口土耳其烟斗起家。20世纪90年代转型为雪茄制造商。Flathead（灵感来自哈雷V型双缸发动机）、Pilon（100%尼加拉瓜）和Cameroon是其最标志性的系列。2007年被通用雪茄收购。', `history_ar` = 'CAO — اختصار اسم كانو أوزغنر المؤسِّس التركي-الأمريكي — وُلد في ناشفيل عام 1968 مستوردًا للغلايين التركية. في التسعينيات تحوَّل إلى صناعة السيجار. الفلات هيد (مستوحى من محركات هارلي V-تويين) والبيلون (100% نيكاراغوا) والكاميرون أكثر تشكيلاته رمزية. استُحوذ عليها General Cigar عام 2007.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. Notes of milk chocolate, hazelnut, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings unique creaminess, slightly sweet on the surface, complex mid-smoke.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"African Cameroon\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Figurado\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin motorcycles, each format named for an engine part. V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notes of leather, black coffee, chocolate, motor oil (really). A road, freedom, industrial America cigar.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100% Nicaraguan — a political statement in a multi-country blend world. Wrapper, binder, filler: all Nicaragua. Notes of pure coffee, cocoa, black pepper. The range for Nicaraguan terroir purists.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Pyramid\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. Notas de milk chocolate, avellana, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings unique creaminess, slightly sweet on the surface, complex mid-smoke.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"African Cameroon\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Figurado\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin motorcycles, each format nombrada por an engine part. V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notas de cuero, black café, chocolate, motor oil (really). A road, freedom, industrial America cigar.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100