[{\"name\": \"ACID Kuba Kuba\", \"color\": \"#7B1FA2\", \"story\": \"The infused best-seller — aromas of tea, botanical herbs, floral essence. Robusto format (54 x 127mm). The cigar that introduced millions of Americans to cigars without intimidating them with traditional blend power. Indonesian wrapper over Drew Estate proprietary blend. Controversial among purists, adored by fans.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Kuba Kuba\", \"Blondie\", \"Dirty Rat\", \"Deep Dish\", \"Krush\"]}, {\"name\": \"Liga Privada No.9\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Drew Estate\'s other face — the most serious, most sought-after. Connecticut Broadleaf Habano wrapper over triple Nicaraguan ligero. تقييم Cigar Aficionado 97. نكهات:  قهوة ريستريتو, 90% cocoa, mulberry. The Flying Pig (short, stout Perfecto format) is the range\'s rarest and most expensive.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Broadleaf Habano\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Robusto\", \"Flying Pig\", \"Petit Lancero\", \"No.9 Perfecto\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 97, \"year\": 2018}]}, {\"name\": \"Undercrown\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Created by the torcedores themselves — factory workers who wanted a cigar as good as Liga Privada at an accessible price. Blend close to the No.9, less expensive Ecuadorian wrapper. نكهات:  شوكولاتة, قهوة, فلفل. The most successful worker rebellion in the industry.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona Viva\", \"Flying Pig\", \"Shade\", \"Sun Grown\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Jonathan Drew\", \"anecdote\": \"Drew composes his blends in nocturnal sessions after midnight, usually to music. The Liga Privada No.9 was composed \'for fifteen friends\' — it has since been smoked by several million people. He still refuses to divulge the precise origins of the blend\'s tobaccos.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Jonathan Drew\", \"anecdote\": \"Drew composes his blends in nocturnal sessions after midnight, usually to music. The Liga Privada No.9 was composed \'for fifteen friends\' — it has since been fumaba by several million people. He still refuses to divulge the precise origins of the blend\'s tobaccos.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Jonathan Drew\", \"anecdote\": \"Drew composes his blends in nocturnal sessions after midnight, usually to music. The Liga Privada No.9 was composed \'for fifteen friends\' — it has since been rauchte by several million people. He still refuses to divulge the precise origins of the blend\'s tobaccos.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Jonathan Drew\", \"anecdote\": \"Drew composes his blends in nocturnal sessions after midnight, usually to music. The Liga Privada No.9 was composed \'for fifteen friends\' — it has since been smoked by several million people. He still refuses to divulge the precise origins of the blend\'s tobaccos.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Jonathan Drew\", \"anecdote\": \"Drew composes his blends in nocturnal sessions after midnight, usually to music. The Liga Privada No.9 was composed \'for fifteen friends\' — it has since been smoked by several million people. He still refuses to divulge the precise origins of the blend\'s tobaccos.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Brooklyn Black Chocolate Stout\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty New York stout from the founders\' city — a cultural terroir pairing. Twin cocoa notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Woodford Reserve\", \"notes\": \"The elegant Kentucky bourbon accompanies the Liga Privada No.9 while highlighting vanilla and oak notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"18-hour cold brew\", \"notes\": \"Cold brew reveals fruity notes in the No.9 that espresso masks. A connoisseur\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Cerveza\", \"name\": \"Brooklyn Black Chocolate Stout\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty New York stout from the founders\' city — a cultural terroir pairing. Twin cocoa notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Woodford Reserve\", \"notes\": \"The elegant Kentucky bourbon accompanies the Liga Privada No.9 while highlighting vanilla and oak notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"18-hour cold brew\", \"notes\": \"Cold brew reveals fruity notes in the No.9 that espresso masks. A connoisseur\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Bier\", \"name\": \"Brooklyn Black Chocolate Stout\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty New York stout from the founders\' city — a cultural terroir pairing. Twin cocoa notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Woodford Reserve\", \"notes\": \"The elegant Kentucky bourbon accompanies the Liga Privada No.9 while highlighting vanilla and oak notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"18-hour cold brew\", \"notes\": \"Cold brew reveals fruity notes in the No.9 that espresso masks. A connoisseur\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"啤酒\", \"name\": \"Brooklyn Black Chocolate Stout\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty New York stout from the founders\' city — a cultural terroir pairing. Twin cocoa notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"波旁威士忌\", \"name\": \"Woodford Reserve\", \"notes\": \"The elegant Kentucky bourbon accompanies the Liga Privada No.9 while highlighting vanilla and oak notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"18-hour cold brew\", \"notes\": \"Cold brew reveals fruity notes in the No.9 that espresso masks. A connoisseur\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"البيرة\", \"name\": \"Brooklyn Black Chocolate Stout\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty New York stout from the founders\' city — a cultural terroir pairing. Twin cocoa notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"البوربون\", \"name\": \"Woodford Reserve\", \"notes\": \"The elegant Kentucky bourbon accompanies the Liga Privada No.9 while highlighting vanilla and oak notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"18-hour cold brew\", \"notes\": \"Cold brew reveals fruity notes in the No.9 that espresso masks. A connoisseur\'s pairing.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Drew Estate';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Excalibur was born from a collaboration that seems improbable on paper: a Swiss entrepreneur (Villiger Söhne), a genius Dominican blender (Hendrik Kelner), and Honduran plantations from the Eiroa family in the Jamastran valley.\r\n\r\nHeinrich Villiger initiated the project in the early 1980s, when the American market was searching for alternatives to the inaccessible Cuban cigars. Kelner — who would later become the driving force behind Davidoff Dominican, Santa Damiana, and a dozen other brands — assembled a Honduran blend exploiting the Corojo tobaccos of Jamastran. Its signature: earthy and deep like Honduras, but with a roundness and creaminess that bring the profile closer to accessible medium territory.\r\n\r\nExcalibur experienced a first period of glory in the 1980s-1990s on the American market, perceived as a quality proxy for forbidden Cuban cigars. Its Robusto earned Cigar Aficionado scores that placed it several times in annual top rankings.\r\n\r\nThe brand was sold to Altadis USA in the early 2000s, but Villiger retained the European rights — creating a dual-market situation comparable to the great Cuban brands under embargo. The Honduran version remains the reference: more earthy, more complex, with the Jamastran signature that distinguishes Honduras from other Central American terroirs. The construction, inherited from Kelner\'s standards, remains exemplary in its consistency.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Excalibur No. I\", \"color\": \"#5C3317\", \"story\": \"The Churchill (49×178mm) that established the brand\'s reputation. Notes of wet earth, white pepper, caramel, and cedar over 90 minutes. The complete demonstration of the Jamastran terroir in a format that reveals all its phases.\"}, {\"name\": \"Excalibur Robusto\", \"color\": \"#7A4520\", \"story\": \"The most popular format (50×124mm) — 45 minutes, immediate earthy and spiced profile. Regular Cigar Aficionado Top 25 appearances. The accessible Honduran reference for enthusiasts seeking body without extremism.\"}, {\"name\": \"Excalibur Dark Knight Maduro\", \"color\": \"#2C1A0E\", \"story\": \"Mexican San Andrés wrapper — dark chocolate, espresso, deep spice notes. Honduras\'s answer to the Maduro trend: less sweet than Cuban Maduros, more earthy, more direct.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Hendrik Kelner\", \"anecdote\": \"Kelner describes Excalibur as \'the project that taught me what Honduras was truly capable of\'. The Jamastran valley was not yet recognized as a major production region in 1983. Excalibur helped establish its international reputation.\"}, {\"name\": \"Heinrich Villiger\", \"anecdote\": \"The Swiss patriarch considered Excalibur his greatest pride in premium cigars. He smoked it daily and categorically refused requests to reformulate the blend in order to reduce costs.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Martinique Aged Agricole Rum 12 Years\", \"notes\": \"The definitive terroir pairing — Martinique sugarcane against Jamastran tobacco, two tropical mountain agricultures. The vegetal richness of agricole rum amplifies the earthy depth of the Excalibur.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Honduras Marcala AOC Coffee\", \"notes\": \"Marcala coffee — one of Honduras\'s rare appellations of origin — shares the same volcanic terroir as the Jamastran tobacco. The ultimate Honduran terroir pairing.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Excalibur';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The General Cigar story begins in Tampa in 1906, in the cigar factories of Ybor City — the Cuban exile neighborhood that had made Tampa the American cigar capital in the 1880s. The original General Cigar Company was a consolidation vehicle from its first years, acquiring smaller Tampa manufacturers whose individual operations were increasingly uncompetitive against the larger houses. The pattern of growth through acquisition was established at the founding and has defined the company ever since.\r\n\r\nThe mid-century transformation moved General Cigar from Tampa manufacturer to national distributor and brand manager. The acquisition of Macanudo in the 1970s provided the brand that would drive the company through the cigar boom of the 1990s — a brand positioned for accessibility and consistency that became, by the early 1980s, the best-selling premium cigar in the United States. Macanudo\'s commercial success funded the acquisitions that followed.\r\n\r\nThe CAO acquisition in 2007 added the premium innovative brand that General Cigar\'s portfolio required. Where Macanudo sold reliability, CAO sold discovery — new formats, unexpected blends, releases that enthusiasts anticipated rather than took for granted. The two brands operate in the same general price tier but target different psychological needs, allowing General Cigar to capture a broader segment of the premium market than either brand could reach alone.\r\n\r\nThe company\'s portfolio now includes cigars under over twenty brand names, produced across manufacturing facilities in the Dominican Republic, Honduras, Jamaica, and Nicaragua. The management challenge — maintaining the distinctive identity and quality standard of each brand while pooling sourcing, logistics, and distribution resources — is the central operational problem of managing a multi-brand cigar company, and General Cigar\'s performance across decades suggests it has developed approaches to this problem that smaller competitors have not.\r\n\r\nThe Scandinavian Tobacco Group, which acquired General Cigar in 2016, added European distribution and manufacturing capabilities that have extended the company\'s reach into markets where American cigar brands had previously operated at a disadvantage.', `history_es` = 'General Cigar es el mayor éxito industrial de la historia del cigarro americano. Fundada en 1906 en Tampa — entonces capital mundial del cigarro — construida a través de adquisiciones sucesivas hasta convertirse en el mayor grupo cigarrero de EE.UU. Su catálogo incluye Macanudo, CAO, Punch, Partagás USA, y docenas más.', `history_de` = 'General Cigar ist der größte industrielle Erfolg der amerikanischen Zigarrengeschichte. 1906 in Tampa gegründet — damals die Welthauptstadt der Zigarre — durch sukzessive Übernahmen zur größten amerikanischen Zigarrengruppe gewachsen. Ihr Katalog umfasst Macanudo, CAO, Punch, Partagás USA und Dutzende mehr.', `history_zh` = '通用雪茄是美国雪茄史上最伟大的工业成就。1906年在坦帕创立——当时的世界雪茄之都——通过连续收购成长为美国最大雪茄集团。其产品目录包括Macanudo、CAO、Punch、美国帕特加斯等数十个品牌。', `history_ar` = 'جنرال سيغار هي أعظم نجاح صناعي في تاريخ السيجار الأمريكي. تأسست عام 1906 في تامبا — عاصمة السيجار العالمية آنذاك — ونمت عبر عمليات استحواذ متتالية لتصبح أكبر مجموعة سيجار أمريكية. كتالوجها يضم ماكانودو وكاو وبنش وعشرات سواها.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Macanudo Café\", \"color\": \"#C9A96E\", \"story\": \"America\'s best-seller for 30 years. Connecticut Shade wrapper, soft and creamy, over Dominican-Jamaican blend. Notes of cream, light cedar, hazelnut. The cigar of sunny terraces and unhurried afternoons. Consistent, accessible, never disappointing.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Café\", \"Baron de Rothschild\", \"Hyde Park\", \"Hampton Court\", \"Prince Philip\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Series inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin engines. Format names: V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notes of motorcycle leather, black coffee, chocolate, engine oil (really). A cigar of the open road, freedom, deep America.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Punch Upper Cut\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The premium General Cigar range under the Punch label. Honduran maduro wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Notes of dark chocolate, smoky wood, pepper. The dark side of Punch — powerful where the classic range is accessible.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Macanudo Café\", \"color\": \"#C9A96E\", \"story\": \"America\'s best-seller for 30 years. Connecticut Shade wrapper, soft and creamy, over Dominican-Jamaican blend. Notas de cream, light cedro, avellana. The cigar of sunny terraces and unhurried afternoons. Consistent, accessible, never disappointing.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Café\", \"Baron de Rothschild\", \"Hyde Park\", \"Hampton Court\", \"Prince Philip\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Series inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin engines. Format names: V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notas de motorcycle cuero, black café, chocolate, engine oil (really). A cigar of the open road, freedom, deep America.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Punch Upper Cut\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The premium General Cigar range under the Punch label. Honduran maduro wr