Experts recommend starting here before venturing toward the Churchill.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Exhibición No.4\", \"Exhibición No.3\"]}, {\"name\": \"Wide Churchill\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"Thick format (55 x 178mm), same length as the Churchill but ring gauge 55 — one of the widest ever produced in Cuba. The increased wrapper surface intensifies the creamy and فانيليا notes. Smoked in 60 دقيقة. Reserved for المتحمسون who do not compromise on ring gauge.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Wide Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Regional Editions\", \"color\": \"#9B2335\", \"story\": \"Romeo y Julieta produces annual regional editions exclusively for different markets — Germany, Spain, UK, Benelux. The Cazadores EL (2018, Germany) and Short Churchills EL are particularly sought after. Some الجامعون travel across Europe solely to acquire local regional editions.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Variable\", \"vitolas\": [\"Cazadores\", \"Short Churchill\", \"Coloniales\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"anecdote\": \"Churchill smoked his first Romeo y Julieta at 21 in Cuba and never stopped. He smoked 8 to 10 cigars per day. His doctor warned him — Churchill replied: \'My doctor told me to stop having dinners. We parted ways.\' He died at 90, cigar in hand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Clark Gable\", \"anecdote\": \"The Hollywood actor had his Romeo y Julieta delivered directly to MGM Studios. During the filming of Gone with the Wind, he reportedly smoked over 300 cigars.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"anecdote\": \"Churchill fumaba his first Romeo y Julieta at 21 in Cuba and never stopped. He fumaba 8 to 10 cigars per day. His doctor warned him — Churchill replied: \'My doctor told me to stop having dinners. We parted ways.\' Murió a los 90, cigar in hand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Clark Gable\", \"anecdote\": \"The Hollywood actor had his Romeo y Julieta delivered directly to MGM Studios. During the filming of Gone with the Wind, he supuestamente fumaba over 300 cigars.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"anecdote\": \"Churchill rauchte his first Romeo y Julieta at 21 in Cuba and never stopped. He rauchte 8 to 10 cigars per day. His doctor warned him — Churchill replied: \'My doctor told me to stop having dinners. We parted ways.\' Er starb im Alter von 90, cigar in hand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Clark Gable\", \"anecdote\": \"The Hollywood actor had his Romeo y Julieta delivered directly to MGM Studios. During the filming of Gone with the Wind, he angeblich rauchte over 300 cigars.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"anecdote\": \"Churchill smoked his first Romeo y Julieta at 21 in Cuba and never stopped. He smoked 8 to 10 cigars per day. His doctor warned him — Churchill replied: \'My doctor told me to stop having dinners. We parted ways.\' 他以 90, cigar in hand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Clark Gable\", \"anecdote\": \"The Hollywood actor had his Romeo y Julieta delivered directly to MGM Studios. During the filming of Gone with the Wind, he 据报道 smoked over 300 cigars.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"anecdote\": \"Churchill smoked his first Romeo y Julieta at 21 in Cuba and never stopped. He smoked 8 to 10 cigars per day. His doctor warned him — Churchill replied: \'My doctor told me to stop having dinners. We parted ways.\' توفي عن عمر 90, cigar in hand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Clark Gable\", \"anecdote\": \"The Hollywood actor had his Romeo y Julieta delivered directly to MGM Studios. During the filming of Gone with the Wind, he يُقال إن smoked over 300 cigars.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Champagne\", \"name\": \"Bollinger R.D. 2007\", \"notes\": \"The fine bubble and minerality of Bollinger sublimate the floral notes of the Churchill in an accord of absolute elegance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Whisky\", \"name\": \"Springbank 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The slight peat and salt of Springbank perfectly counterbalance the creamy sweetness of a Romeo y Julieta.\"}, {\"type\": \"Tea\", \"name\": \"Darjeeling First Flush\", \"notes\": \"The world\'s most floral tea meets Cuba\'s most floral cigar. A delicate pairing reserved for sunny afternoons.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Champán\", \"name\": \"Bollinger R.D. 2007\", \"notes\": \"The fine bubble and minerality of Bollinger sublimate the floral notas de the Churchill in an accord of absolute elegance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Whisky\", \"name\": \"Springbank 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The slight peat and salt of Springbank perfectly counterbalance the creamy sweetness of a Romeo y Julieta.\"}, {\"type\": \"Té\", \"name\": \"Darjeeling First Flush\", \"notes\": \"The world\'s most floral tea meets Cuba\'s most floral cigar. A delicate pairing reserved for sunny afternoons.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Champagner\", \"name\": \"Bollinger R.D. 2007\", \"notes\": \"The fine bubble and minerality of Bollinger sublimate the floral Noten von the Churchill in an accord of absolute elegance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Whisky\", \"name\": \"Springbank 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The slight peat and salt of Springbank perfectly counterbalance the creamy sweetness of a Romeo y Julieta.\"}, {\"type\": \"Tee\", \"name\": \"Darjeeling First Flush\", \"notes\": \"The world\'s most floral tea meets Cuba\'s most floral cigar. A delicate pairing reserved for sunny afternoons.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"香槟\", \"name\": \"Bollinger R.D. 2007\", \"notes\": \"The fine bubble and minerality of Bollinger sublimate the floral 风味： the Churchill in an accord of absolute elegance.\"}, {\"type\": \"威士忌\", \"name\": \"Springbank 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The slight peat and salt of Springbank perfectly counterbalance the creamy sweetness of a Romeo y Julieta.\"}, {\"type\": \"茶\", \"name\": \"Darjeeling First Flush\", \"notes\": \"The world\'s most floral tea meets Cuba\'s most floral cigar. A delicate pairing reserved for sunny afternoons.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"الشامبانيا\", \"name\": \"Bollinger R.D. 2007\", \"notes\": \"The fine bubble and minerality of Bollinger sublimate the floral نكهات: the Churchill in an accord of absolute elegance.\"}, {\"type\": \"الويسكي\", \"name\": \"Springbank 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The slight peat and salt of Springbank perfectly counterbalance the creamy sweetness of a Romeo y Julieta.\"}, {\"type\": \"الشاي\", \"name\": \"Darjeeling First Flush\", \"notes\": \"The world\'s most floral tea meets Cuba\'s most floral cigar. A delicate pairing reserved for sunny afternoons.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Romeo y Julieta';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The American Romeo y Julieta shares with Cohiba USA and Partagás USA the same legal genesis: the American embargo against Cuba opened the way for trademark registration on American soil by entities entirely distinct from the original Havana house.\r\n\r\nAltadis USA (now Imperial Brands) holds the American rights to Romeo y Julieta and produces the range in the Dominican Republic. The American brand has succeeded in creating its own identity without trying to exactly reproduce the Cuban profile — a judicious strategic choice that spared it the inevitable unfavorable comparisons.\r\n\r\nThe 1875 range — the number recalling the founding year of the original Havana house — is built around Dominican and Ecuadorian tobaccos with Nicaraguan contributions. Its softer, creamier profile than the Cuban version reflects the preferences of the broad American market, allowing it to reach volumes the Cuban brand will never approach.\r\n\r\nThe Reserve Maduro is the most ambitious interpretation of the American brand. Using a Connecticut Broadleaf wrapper fermented two years, it develops milk chocolate and roasted coffee and has regularly appeared in Cigar Aficionado\'s Top 25. Several serious enthusiasts argue it deserves to be evaluated independently of its Cuban namesake — not as a substitute, but as an expression of a distinct aesthetic.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Romeo y Julieta 1875\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"Entry premium range — Dominican Connecticut wrapper on Santo Domingo blend. Creamy, soft, accessible. Notes of hazelnut, light wood, soft spices. The American Romeo y Julieta for the daily smoker.\"}, {\"name\": \"Romeo y Julieta Reserve\", \"color\": \"#5C1A1A\", \"story\": \"Medium range — Ecuador wrapper on enriched Nicaraguan blend. More body and complexity than the 1875, with cedar, white pepper, and coffee. For enthusiasts finding the 1875 too light.\"}, {\"name\": \"Romeo y Julieta Reserve Maduro\", \"color\": \"#2C0A0A\", \"story\": \"The range\'s masterpiece — Connecticut Broadleaf wrapper fermented 2 years. Milk chocolate, roasted coffee, dark caramel. Multiple Cigar Aficionado Top 25 appearances. Proof that the American brand has developed its own identity of excellence.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"American national distribution\", \"anecdote\": \"Romeo y Julieta USA is present in more than 8,000 American retail locations — steakhouses, country clubs, Marriott hotels, airport lounges. This ubiquity made the brand the introduction to premium cigars for millions of Americans who would never have accessed the Cuban original.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Blanton\'s Single Barrel Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"For the Reserve Maduro, the caramel and vanilla of Blanton\'s play perfectly with the chocolate and roasted coffee notes — the classic American pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Wine\", \"name\": \"Napa Valley Cabernet Sauvignon\", \"notes\": \"The tannic structure of a Napa Cab pairs with the robustness of the Reserve Maduro for a premium American pairing typical of the great Sonoma cellars.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Romeo y Julieta USA';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Santa Damiana embodies a rare proposition in the premium cigar industry: softness as an absolute value, without concession to the power trend that has dominated the market since the 1990s. Founded in 1993 in La Romana, the brand was created by Hendrik Kelner — the legendary blender of Tabacalera de García — for a clientele seeking elegance without intensity.\r\n\r\nSanta Damiana\'s philosophy is explicitly anti-trend. While the 2000s saw a generalized race toward stronger, more Nicaraguan, more maduro blends, the brand maintained its reference position in the soft-medium register: Connecticut Shade wrapper, balanced Dominican blend, light to medium strength.\r\n\r\nThis apparent conservatism conceals real sophistication. As Kelner himself has stated publicly: \"Building an interesting cigar without power is technically more difficult than assembling an aromatic bomb. With power, you can hide many mistakes.\" Santa Damiana\'s consistency over three decades validates this claim.\r\n\r\nGolf enthusiasts have particularly adopted Santa Damiana: light for 18 holes, built for the outdoors, accessible pricing for daily consumption. This association with American and European premium golf has given the brand visibility in country clubs that far exceeds its presence in traditional cigar bars.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Santa Damiana Cabinet Selection\", \"color\": \"#D4A96A\", \"story\": \"The flagship proposition — Connecticut Shade wrapper on pure Dominican blend. Notes of cream, hazelnut, white cedar. 45 minutes of light sophistication. The quintessential premium golf cigar.\"}, {\"name\": \"Santa Damiana Selección No. 800\", \"color\": \"#C49A6C\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper on Dominican blend extended with a few percent Nicaraguan. Slightly more body than the Cabinet, with roasted hazelnut and milk chocolate. Still in the soft register but with more complexity.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Hendrik Kelner\", \"anecdote\": \"The blender behind Santa Damiana — and Davidoff Dominican, Avo, and a dozen other brands — is one of the least publicized and most influential tobacco technicians in the industry. \'A great soft cigar is infinitely more difficult to create than a great powerful cigar\', he has repeated for thirty years.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Wine\", \"name\": \"Champagne Blanc de Blancs\", \"notes\": \"The brand\'s most elegant pairing — the mineral lightness of a Blanc de Blancs Champagne with the Connecticut Shade creaminess. The exceptional aperitif of European country clubs.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Soft café au lait\", \"notes\": \"The perfect daily pairing for the Cabinet Selection. The milky sweetness amplified by the creamy lightness of the wrapper — two products designed for morning comfort.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Santa Damiana';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The history of Tabacalera de Filipinas begins not with an entrepreneurial decision but with a colonial administrative one. In 1881, the Spanish crown dissolved the Real Compañía de Filipinas — the state tobacco monopoly that had controlled Philippine tobacco production, distribution, and export since the eighteenth century — and authorized the creation of private manufacturers to operate in its place. The transition from monopoly to competitive production was designed to modernize an industry that had grown bureaucratically rigid, and Tabacalera emerged from this reorganization as the largest and best-capitalized of the new private manufacturers.\r\n\r\nThe Spanish colonial administration had cultivated Philippine tobacco specifically for export to Spain for over two centuries before this moment. The Cagayan Valley in northern Luzon — the primary growing region then and now — had been mapped, its tobaccos classified, and its cultivation practices systematized through decades of monopoly management. The Ilocos region\'s leaf, grown under different conditions on the northwestern coast, provided a complementary variety that blenders used to adjust profiles. The technical knowledge embedded in the industry was substantial, if bureaucratically constrained.\r\n\r\nWhat makes Philippine tobacco genuinely distinct in the world context is difficult to describe without the vocabulary of tasting, but it is real and consistent. The retrohale — the aromatic return through the nasal passage when exhaling — carries notes that experienced tasters describe as mentholated, cooling, slightly floral. This is not a variety characteristic or a fermentation artifact but an expression of the Cagayan soil\'s chemistry and the particular way Philippine tobacco metabolizes its alkaloids. No other major growing region produces it, and blenders who seek it have historically had no choice but to source from the Philippines.\r\n\r\nThe company\'s ownership has changed several times since independence — Spanish interests were replaced by Filipino shareholders after 1946, and the ownership structure has evolved through the subsequent decades. The Cagayan Valley source material and the original manufacturing practices in Agoo, La Union, have remained continuous throughout these transitions.', `history_es` = 'Tabacalera de Filipinas fue fundada en 1881 por decreto real español — el monopolio colonial del tabaco transformado en fábrica privada. Es la más antigua de Asia del Sudeste. El tabaco del Valle de Cagayan crea cigarros de perfil único: más ligeros, herbáceos, ligeramente mentolados en el retrogusto. Un terroir verdaderamente único en el mundo.', `history_de` = 'Tabacalera de Filipinas wurde 1881 durch königlichen spanischen Erlass gegründet — das koloniale Tabakmonopol in eine Privatfabrik umgewandelt. Es ist die älteste in Südostasien. Der Tabak des Cagayan-Tals schafft Zigarren mit einzigartigem Profil: leichter, krautig, im Abgang leicht mentholiert. Ein wirklich einzigartiges Terroir der Welt.', `history_zh` = '菲律宾烟草公司于1881年由西班牙皇室法令创立——殖民地烟草垄断企业转变为私营工厂。它是东南亚最古老的。卡加延谷地的烟草创造了具有独特轮廓的雪茄：更轻盈、更草本、回味略带薄荷味。世界上真正独一无二的风土。', `history_ar` = 'تأسست تاباكاليرا دي فيليبيناس عام 1881 بمرسوم ملكي إسباني — تحويل احتكار التبغ الاستعماري إلى مصنع خاص. إنها الأقدم في جنوب شرق آسيا. تبغ وادي كاغايان يُنتج سيجارًا بملف فريد: أخف، عشبي، مع نفحة نعناعية في النهاية. تربة فريدة حقًا في العالم.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Tabacalera Premium\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The current flagship — 2-year-aged Cagayan tobacco. Herbaceous notes, slightly mentholated, light wood. Light-Medium, very accessible. The Philippine reference cigar for enthusiasts curious to explore non-Caribbean terroirs. Churchill format recommended for a complete aromatic evolution.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Cagayan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Double Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"La Flor de la Isabela\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Founded simultaneously with Tabacalera in 1881, this sister brand was named for Queen Isabella II of Spain. The two brands share the same Cagayan factory and plantations. La Flor de la Isabela is often considered the finest expression of Philippine tobacco — light, floral, unique.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Ilocos\", \"vitolas\": [\"Corona\", \"Panetela\", \"Cigarito\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Tabacalera Premium\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The current flagship — 2-year-aged Cagayan tobacco. Herbaceous notes, slightly mentholated, light wood. Light-Medium, very accessible. The Philippine reference cigar for aficionados curious to explore non-Caribbean terroirs. Churchill format recommended for a complete aromatic evolution.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Cagayan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Double Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"La Flor de la Isabela\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Founded simultaneously with Tabacalera in 1881, this sister brand was nombrada por Queen Isabella II of Spain. The two brands share the same Cagayan factory and plantations. La Flor de la Isabela is often considerado the finest expression of Philippine tobacco — light, floral, unique.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Ilocos\", \"vitolas\": [\"Corona\", \"Panetela\", \"Cigarito\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Tabacalera Premium\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The current flagship — 2-year-aged Cagayan tobacco. Herbaceous notes, slightly mentholated, light wood. Light-Medium, very accessible. The Philippine reference cigar for enthusiasts curious to explore non-Caribbean terroirs. Churchill format recommended for a complete aromatic evolution.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Cagayan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Double Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"La Flor de la Isabela\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Founded simultaneously with Tabacalera in 1881, this sister brand was benannt nach Queen Isabella II of Spain. The two brands share the same Cagayan factory and plantations. La Flor de la Isabela is often considered the finest expression of Philippine tobacco — light, floral, unique.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Ilocos\", \"vitolas\": [\"Corona\", \"Panetela\", \"Cigarito\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Tabacalera Premium\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The current flagship — 2-year-aged Cagayan tobacco. Herbaceous notes, slightly mentholated, light wood. Light-Medium, very accessible. The Philippine reference cigar for 爱好者 curious to explore non-Caribbean terroirs. Churchill format recommended for a complete aromatic evolution.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Cagayan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Double Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"La Flor de la Isabela\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Founded simultaneously with Tabacalera in 1881, this sister brand was named for Queen Isabella II of Spain. The two brands share the same Cagayan factory and plantations. La Flor de la Isabela is often considered the finest expression of Philippine tobacco — light, floral, unique.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Ilocos\", \"vitolas\": [\"Corona\", \"Panetela\", \"Cigarito\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Tabacalera Premium\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The current flagship — 2-year-aged Cagayan tobacco. Herbaceous notes, slightly mentholated, light wood. Light-Medium, very accessible. The Philippine reference cigar for المتحمسون curious to explore non-Caribbean terroirs. Churchill format recommended for a complete aromatic evolution.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Cagayan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Double Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"La Flor de la Isabela\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Founded simultaneously with Tabacalera in 1881, this sister brand was named for Queen Isabella II of Spain. The two brands share the same Cagayan factory and plantations. La Flor de la Isabela is often considered the finest expression of Philippine tobacco — light, floral, unique.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Philippine Ilocos\", \"vitolas\": [\"Corona\", \"Panetela\", \"Cigarito\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Spanish Empire\", \"anecdote\": \"The royal tobacco monopoly in the Philippines, established in 1782, was one of the Spanish Empire\'s most important revenue sources in Asia. When the monopoly was lifted in 1881, Tabacalera was born to privatize this infrastructure — and has perpetuated it ever since.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Spanish Empire\", \"anecdote\": \"The royal tobacco monopoly in the Philippines, established in 1782, was one of the Spanish Empire\'s most important revenue sources in Asia. When the monopoly was lifted in 1881, Tabacalera was born to privatize this infrastructure — and has perpetuated it ever since.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Spanish Empire\", \"anecdote\": \"The royal tobacco monopoly in the Philippines, established in 1782, was one of the Spanish Empire\'s most important revenue sources in Asia. When the monopoly was lifted in 1881, Tabacalera was born to privatize this infrastructure — and has perpetuated it ever since.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Spanish Empire\", \"anecdote\": \"The royal tobacco monopoly in the Philippines, established in 1782, was one of the Spanish Empire\'s most important revenue sources in Asia. When the monopoly was lifted in 1881, Tabacalera was born to privatize this infrastructure — and has perpetuated it ever since.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Spanish Empire\", \"anecdote\": \"The royal tobacco monopoly in the Philippines, established in 1782, was one of the Spanish Empire\'s most important revenue sources in Asia. When the monopoly was lifted in 1881, Tabacalera was born to privatize this infrastructure — and has perpetuated it ever since.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Tea\", \"name\": \"Philippine green tea\", \"notes\": \"The green tea from the same islands as the tobacco — shared herbaceous notes, an island terroir pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Tanduay Philippine rum\", \"notes\": \"The Philippines\' national rum, soft and vanilla-flavored, naturally accompanies the herbaceous lightness of a Tabacalera.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Té\", \"name\": \"Philippine green tea\", \"notes\": \"The green tea from the same islands as the tobacco — shared herbaceous notes, an island terroir pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Ron\", \"name\": \"Tanduay Philippine rum\", \"notes\": \"The Philippines\' national rum, soft and vanilla-flavored, acompaña naturalmente the herbaceous lightness of a Tabacalera.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Tee\", \"name\": \"Philippine green tea\", \"notes\": \"The green tea from the same islands as the tobacco — shared herbaceous notes, an island terroir pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Tanduay Philippine rum\", \"notes\": \"The Philippines\' national rum, soft and vanilla-flavored, naturally accompanies the herbaceous lightness of a Tabacalera.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"茶\", \"name\": \"Philippine green tea\", \"notes\": \"The green tea from the same islands as the tobacco — shared herbaceous notes, an island terroir pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"朗姆酒\", \"name\": \"Tanduay Philippine rum\", \"notes\": \"The Philippines\' national rum, soft and vanilla-flavored, naturally accompanies the herbaceous lightness of a Tabacalera.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"الشاي\", \"name\": \"Philippine green tea\", \"notes\": \"The green tea from the same islands as the tobacco — shared herbaceous notes, an island terroir pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"الروم\", \"name\": \"Tanduay Philippine rum\", \"notes\": \"The Philippines\' national rum, soft and vanilla-flavored, naturally accompanies the herbaceous lightness of a Tabacalera.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Tabacalera';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Tobacco cultivation in Mexico\'s Veracruz state predates the arrival of Europeans by millennia. The Totonac people who inhabited the Gulf coast slopes of the Sierra Madre Oriental grew, processed, and smoked tobacco in ceremonial and social contexts that Spanish colonial observers documented with bewilderment and curiosity. When the Spanish established formal tobacco cultivation in the region in the sixteenth century, they were regularizing a practice that the land and the people had already developed to considerable sophistication.\r\n\r\nThe San Andrés Tuxtla subregion, where Te Amo\'s tobacco is grown, produces two varieties of significant commercial importance. The first is a natural wrapper leaf of unusual darkness — not artificially darkened through extended fermentation, but grown in conditions of altitude and humidity that produce natural dark pigmentation in the leaf. San Andrés Natural wrapper provides the visual and aromatic characteristics of a Maduro without requiring the months of additional processing that convert lighter tobaccos to dark. The second is the San Andrés Maduro proper — the same leaf subjected to controlled fermentation that develops its inherent sweetness into a chocolate complexity found in no other wrapper variety at comparable consistency.\r\n\r\nBoth varieties appear in Te Amo\'s production, which spans from accessible everyday formats to the serious premium range that has earned the brand attention in the specialist press. The house\'s commercial position is unusual: it functions simultaneously as a cigar manufacturer and as a tobacco supplier to some of the most significant names in the American market. Arturo Fuente, My Father, Perdomo, and several others have built premium maduro lines specifically around San Andrés leaf — testament to the variety\'s qualities and to Te Amo\'s ability to maintain supply quality across multi-year supplier relationships.\r\n\r\nFounded in 1963 by a cooperative of San Andrés growers who understood their tobacco\'s potential better than their existing commercial intermediaries, Te Amo represents a specific moment in Mexican agricultural industrialization: the point at which primary producers recognized that capturing the manufacturing stage of their product\'s value chain was both possible and necessary.', `history_es` = 'La región de San Andrés Tuxtla, Veracruz, México, cultiva tabaco desde tiempos precolombinos — los totonacos ofrecían cigarros a los dioses. Te Amo, fundada en 1963, es la guardiana de esta tradición milenaria. El tabaco San Andrés Maduro — fermentado por humedad natural — desarrolla una dulzura chocolateada única utilizada en grandes blends maduro mundiales.', `history_de` = 'Die Region San Andrés Tuxtla, Veracruz, Mexiko, baut Tabak seit präkolumbianischer Zeit an — die Totonaken opferten Zigarren den Göttern. Te Amo, 1963 gegründet, ist die Hüterin dieser jahrtausendealten Tradition. Der San Andrés Maduro Tabak — durch natürliche Feuchtigkeit fermentiert — entwickelt eine einzigartige schokoladige Süße, die in großen weltweiten Maduro-Blends verwendet wird.', `history_zh` = '墨西哥韦拉克鲁斯州的圣安德烈斯图斯特拉地区自前哥伦布时代就种植烟草——托托纳克人以雪茄祭神。1963年创立的Te Amo是这一千年传统的守护者。圣安德烈斯马杜罗烟草——通过自然湿度发酵——形成了独特的巧克力甜味，被全球主要马杜罗混合所使用。', `history_ar` = 'تزرع منطقة سان أندريس توستلا بولاية فيراكروز، المكسيك، التبغ منذ العصور ما قبل الكولومبية — كان التوتوناك يقدِّمون السيجار قربانًا للآلهة. تي آمو، المؤسَّسة عام 1963، حارسة هذا التراث الألفي. تبغ سان أندريس مادورو — المخمَّر بالرطوبة الطبيعية — يُنمِّي حلاوة شوكولاتية فريدة مستخدَمة في كبريات خلطات مادورو العالمية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Te Amo Meditation\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Mexican-Nicaraguan blend. Notes of milk chocolate, vanilla, coffee cream. Medium, soft. The paradoxical sweetness of Mexican Maduro: dark in appearance, suave on the palate. Ideal for converting Connecticut Shade enthusiasts to the world of dark wrappers.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Meditation\", \"Torero\", \"Matador\", \"Grande\", \"Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Revolution\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Full body — the powerful side. Mexican San Andrés oscuro wrapper over pure Mexican ligero. Notes of dark chocolate, licorice, volcanic earth. Rare but sought-after, the Revolution reveals the telluric dimension of Veracruz tobacco — the volcanic soil of Mexico in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. Notes of hazelnut, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Te Amo Meditation\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Mexican-Nicaraguan blend. Notas de milk chocolate, vainilla, café cream. Medium, soft. The dulzura paradójica of Mexican Maduro: dark in appearance, suave on the palate. Ideal for converting Connecticut Shade aficionados to the world of dark wrappers.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Meditation\", \"Torero\", \"Matador\", \"Grande\", \"Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Revolution\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Full body — the powerful side. Mexican San Andrés oscuro wrapper over pure Mexican ligero. Notas de chocolate negro, regaliz, volcanic earth. Rare but sought-after, the Revolution revela the telluric dimension of Veracruz tobacco — the volcanic soil of Mexico in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. Notas de avellana, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Te Amo Meditation\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Mexican-Nicaraguan blend. Noten von milk Schokolade, Vanille, Kaffee cream. Medium, soft. The paradoxe Süße of Mexican Maduro: dark in appearance, suave on the palate. Ideal for converting Connecticut Shade enthusiasts to the world of dark wrappers.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Meditation\", \"Torero\", \"Matador\", \"Grande\", \"Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Revolution\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Full body — the powerful side. Mexican San Andrés oscuro wrapper over pure Mexican ligero. Noten von dunkle Schokolade, licorice, volcanic earth. Rare but sought-after, the Revolution reveals the telluric dimension of Veracruz tobacco — the volcanic soil of Mexico in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. Noten von Haselnuss, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Te Amo Meditation\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Mexican-Nicaraguan blend. 风味： milk 巧克力, 香草, 咖啡 cream. Medium, soft. The 矛盾的甜美 of Mexican Maduro: dark in appearance, suave on the palate. Ideal for converting Connecticut Shade 爱好者 to the world of dark wrappers.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Meditation\", \"Torero\", \"Matador\", \"Grande\", \"Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Revolution\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Full body — the powerful side. Mexican San Andrés oscuro wrapper over pure Mexican ligero. 风味： 黑巧克力, 甘草, volcanic earth. Rare but sought-after, the Revolution 展现出 the telluric dimension of Veracruz tobacco — the volcanic soil of Mexico in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. 风味： 榛子, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Te Amo Meditation\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Mexican-Nicaraguan blend. نكهات:  milk شوكولاتة, فانيليا, قهوة cream. Medium, soft. The الحلاوة المتناقضة of Mexican Maduro: dark in appearance, suave on the palate. Ideal for converting Connecticut Shade المتحمسون to the world of dark wrappers.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Meditation\", \"Torero\", \"Matador\", \"Grande\", \"Churchill\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Revolution\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Full body — the powerful side. Mexican San Andrés oscuro wrapper over pure Mexican ligero. نكهات:  شوكولاتة داكنة, عرق السوس, volcanic earth. Rare but sought-after, the Revolution يكشف عن the telluric dimension of Veracruz tobacco — the volcanic soil of Mexico in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. نكهات:  بندق, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty notes of both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty notas de both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty Noten von both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty 风味： both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty نكهات: both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Te Amo';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Trinidad\'s story begins in the most rarefied space in Cuban politics: the personal gift list of Fidel Castro. In 1969, three years after Cohiba was created for Castro\'s own use, a second ultra-premium brand was commissioned for a different purpose — not personal consumption but state diplomacy of the highest order. The brief was precise: a cigar so exceptional that giving it to a head of state would be understood immediately as a gesture of extraordinary esteem. A cigar, in other words, that could not be bought.\r\n\r\nFor 29 years, Trinidad was precisely that. It existed in the cellars of the Cuban foreign ministry and the luggage of diplomatic delegations. It circulated among the heads of the Non-Aligned Movement, the leaders of newly independent African nations, selected European statesmen. Nelson Mandela received it. So did several African heads of state whose support Cuba was courting. So, reportedly, did various figures in European and Latin American politics whose names have never been officially confirmed. Trinidad was statecraft in cedar and tobacco.\r\n\r\nThe format chosen for this period was the Fundadores: 40 x 192mm, the longest Cuban cigar ever produced at commercial scale. Nearly 20 centimeters of pure Vuelta Abajo — a single continuous smoking experience that can last two hours and passes through aromatic phases as distinct as acts in a play. The thinness of the ring gauge produces a cooler, more concentrated draw that amplifies the subtlety of the tobacco rather than its power. It is a cigar that requires full attention and rewards it completely.\r\n\r\nThe public unveiling came in November 1998, at a gala dinner organized by Davidoff in Paris. The announcement that Trinidad would finally be available commercially caused a sensation in the cigar world disproportionate to any marketing campaign. Here was a brand that enthusiasts had been hearing rumors about for three decades — and in some cases had tasted in private, passed along by contacts in diplomatic circles — suddenly placed on the market. The Fundadores sold out immediately and has remained chronically undersupplied ever since.\r\n\r\nTrinidad\'s production remains the smallest of any major Cuban house. The factory allocates a fraction of its capacity to Trinidad, using tobaccos that go through the same rigorous leaf selection process as Cohiba — the closest comparison in the portfolio. The Reyes, a Petit Corona added to the line in 2003, made the brand accessible in a shorter format while preserving the house profile: refined, complex, surprisingly strong for its apparent elegance. The Coloniales, a Corona Extra, sits between the two in both size and character.\r\n\r\nThe brand\'s mystique has not diminished with commercial availability. If anything, the knowledge that Trinidad spent its first three decades as a diplomatic secret has deepened the devotion of its collectors. These are not smokers who came to Trinidad because they saw it reviewed. They came because someone who had been somewhere extraordinary told them, quietly, what they had smoked.', `history_es` = 'Trinidad fue creada en 1969 como regalo diplomático de Estado, igual que Cohiba. Durante 29 años sólo existió en los maletines de los ministros cubanos. En 1998, se lanzó públicamente en una gala de Davidoff en París — con el Fundadores (40x192mm), el cigarro cubano comercial más largo jamás producido. La marca más rara y misteriosa de Cuba.', `history_de` = 'Trinidad wurde 1969 als staatliches diplomatisches Geschenk geschaffen, genau wie Cohiba. Achtundzwanzig Jahre lang existierte sie nur in den Aktentaschen kubanischer Minister. 1998 wurde sie bei einer Davidoff-Gala in Paris öffentlich vorgestellt — mit dem Fundadores (40x192mm), der längsten je produzierten kubanischen Zigarre.', `history_zh` = '特立尼达于1969年作为国家外交礼物创立，与科伊巴一样。29年间它只存在于古巴部长们的公文包里。1998年在大卫杜夫巴黎晚宴上公开发布——推出了Fundadores（40×192mm），有史以来商业生产的最长古巴雪茄。古巴最稀有、最神秘的品牌。', `history_ar` = 'أُنشئت ترينيداد عام 1969 هدية دبلوماسية من الدولة، شأنها شأن كوهيبا. ظلت 29 عامًا حكرًا على حقائب الوزراء الكوبيين. عام 1998 أُطلقت علنًا في حفل ديفيدوف بباريس — مع فوندادوريس (40×192ملم)، أطول سيجار كوبي تجاري أُنتج على الإطلاق. أندر وأغمض علامة كوبية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Notes of fresh cedar, white flowers, rock honey.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considered the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 minutes, it delivers all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it reveals a bolder, spicier profile than the house\'s thin formats. Notes of cinnamon, ebony, coffee. A surprise for Fundadores enthusiasts discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Notas de fresh cedro, white flowers, rock miel.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considerado the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 minutes, it ofrece all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it revela a bolder, spicier profile than la thin formats. Notas de canela, ebony, café. A surprise for Fundadores aficionados discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Noten von fresh Zeder, white flowers, rock honey.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considered the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 minutes, it delivers all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it reveals a bolder, spicier profile than the house\'s thin formats. Noten von cinnamon, ebony, Kaffee. A surprise for Fundadores enthusiasts discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 分钟 of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. 风味： fresh 雪松木, white flowers, rock honey.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considered the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 分钟, it 带来 all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it 展现出 a bolder, spicier profile than the house\'s thin formats. 风味： 肉桂, ebony, 咖啡. A surprise for Fundadores 爱好者 discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 دقيقة of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. نكهات:  fresh أرز, white flowers, rock honey.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considered the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 دقيقة, it يمنح all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it يكشف عن a bolder, spicier profile than the house\'s thin formats. نكهات:  قرفة, ebony, قهوة. A surprise for Fundadores المتحمسون discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Nelson Mandela\", \"anecdote\": \"Among the first recipients of Trinidad diplomatic cigars, Mandela received boxes during his visits to Cuba. Whether he smoked them personally is undocumented, but Trinidads circulated in his inner circle.\"}, {\"name\": \"Alain Ducasse\", \"anecdote\": \"The starred chef, a great cigar enthusiast, reportedly described the Fundadores as \'the cigar closest to a great Burgundy wine\' — same rarity, same delicacy, same ingratitude if poorly treated.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Nelson Mandela\", \"anecdote\": \"Among the first recipients of Trinidad diplomatic cigars, Mandela received boxes during his visits to Cuba. Whether he fumaba them personally is undocumented, but Trinidads circulated in his inner circle.\"}, {\"name\": \"Alain Ducasse\", \"anecdote\": \"The starred chef, a great cigar enthusiast, supuestamente described the Fundadores as \'the cigar closest to a great Burgundy wine\' — same rarity, same delicacy, same ingratitude if poorly treated.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Nelson Mandela\", \"anecdote\": \"Among the first recipients of Trinidad diplomatic cigars, Mandela received boxes during his visits to Cuba. Whether he rauchte them personally is undocumented, but Trinidads circulated in his inner circle.\"}, {\"name\": \"Alain Ducasse\", \"anecdote\": \"The starred chef, a great cigar enthusiast, angeblich described the Fundadores as \'the cigar closest to a great Burgundy wine\' — same rarity, same delicacy, same ingratitude if poorly treated.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Nelson Mandela\", \"anecdote\": \"Among the first recipients of Trinidad diplomatic cigars, Mandela received boxes during his visits to Cuba. Whether he smoked them personally is undocumented, but Trinidads circulated in his inner circle.\"}, {\"name\": \"Alain Ducasse\", \"anecdote\": \"The starred chef, a great cigar enthusiast, 据报道 described the Fundadores as \'the cigar closest to a great Burgundy wine\' — same rarity, same delicacy, same ingratitude if poorly treated.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Nelson Mandela\", \"anecdote\": \"Among the first recipients of Trinidad diplomatic cigars, Mandela received boxes during his visits to Cuba. Whether he smoked them personally is undocumented, but Trinidads circulated in his inner circle.\"}, {\"name\": \"Alain Ducasse\", \"anecdote\": \"The starred chef, a great cigar enthusiast, يُقال إن described the Fundadores as \'the cigar closest to a great Burgundy wine\' — same rarity, same delicacy, same ingratitude if poorly treated.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Wine\", \"name\": \"Chambolle-Musigny Premier Cru\", \"notes\": \"The floral delicacy and silky length of a great Chambolle find a perfect echo in the white flower notes of the Fundadores. The most distinguished pairing that exists.\"}, {\"type\": \"Champagne\", \"name\": \"Krug Grande Cuvée\", \"notes\": \"The complexity and finesse of Krug naturally accompany the elegant mystery of a Trinidad Reyes. A pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Vintage Armagnac 1985\", \"notes\": \"A vintage from the same year as the first commercially released Trinidads — a collector\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Vino\", \"name\": \"Chambolle-Musigny Premier Cru\", \"notes\": \"The floral delicacy and silky length of a great Chambolle find a perfect echo in the white flower notas de the Fundadores. The most distinguished pairing that exists.\"}, {\"type\": \"Champán\", \"name\": \"Krug Grande Cuvée\", \"notes\": \"The complexity and finesse of Krug naturally accompany the elegant mystery of a Trinidad Reyes. A pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"Licores\", \"name\": \"Vintage Armagnac 1985\", \"notes\": \"A vintage from the same year as the first commercially released Trinidads — a collector\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Wein\", \"name\": \"Chambolle-Musigny Premier Cru\", \"notes\": \"The floral delicacy and silky length of a great Chambolle find a perfect echo in the white flower Noten von the Fundadores. The most distinguished pairing that exists.\"}, {\"type\": \"Champagner\", \"name\": \"Krug Grande Cuvée\", \"notes\": \"The complexity and finesse of Krug naturally accompany the elegant mystery of a Trinidad Reyes. A pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"Spirituosen\", \"name\": \"Vintage Armagnac 1985\", \"notes\": \"A vintage from the same year as the first commercially released Trinidads — a collector\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"葡萄酒\", \"name\": \"Chambolle-Musigny Premier Cru\", \"notes\": \"The floral delicacy and silky length of a great Chambolle find a perfect echo in the white flower 风味： the Fundadores. The most distinguished pairing that exists.\"}, {\"type\": \"香槟\", \"name\": \"Krug Grande Cuvée\", \"notes\": \"The complexity and finesse of Krug naturally accompany the elegant mystery of a Trinidad Reyes. A pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"烈酒\", \"name\": \"Vintage Armagnac 1985\", \"notes\": \"A vintage from the same year as the first commercially released Trinidads — a collector\'s pairing.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"النبيذ\", \"name\": \"Chambolle-Musigny Premier Cru\", \"notes\": \"The floral delicacy and silky length of a great Chambolle find a perfect echo in the white flower نكهات: the Fundadores. The most distinguished pairing that exists.\"}, {\"type\": \"الشامبانيا\", \"name\": \"Krug Grande Cuvée\", \"notes\": \"The complexity and finesse of Krug naturally accompany the elegant mystery of a Trinidad Reyes. A pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"المسكرات\", \"name\": \"Vintage Armagnac 1985\", \"notes\": \"A vintage from the same year as the first commercially released Trinidads — a collector\'s pairing.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Trinidad';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Vegas Robaina is the only Cuban cigar brand to bear the name of a veguero — a tobacco grower — rather than a manufacturer, a historical figure, or a place. Alejandro Robaina, born in 1919 in the Vuelta Abajo region, inherited the family lands of San Luis and cultivated them with methodical obstinacy for more than sixty years.\r\n\r\nThe story of Don Alejandro is one of a reputation built leaf by leaf, without any communication strategy, on the sole quality of the tobacco. His colorado maduro wrappers — dark, oily, of remarkable textural consistency — were purchased at premium prices by the greatest Havana manufacturers since the 1950s. Cohiba, Montecristo, Partagás all sourced Robaina tobacco without the public knowing anything about it.\r\n\r\nIn 1997, Habanos S.A. made the radically unusual choice to create a brand bearing his name — publicly acknowledging what Cuban commerce had known for decades. Don Alejandro was 78 years old when the brand launched. He died in 2010 at age 91, surrounded by his plantations.\r\n\r\nVegas Robaina produces in extremely limited quantities. The manufacture uses only leaves from the Robaina family properties in San Luis — a geographical constraint that forbids any significant production increase. The Don Alejandro (Gran Corona 55×180mm) is one of the most sought-after and least readily available Cuban formats outside Cuba itself. Hiroshi Robaina, the grandson, perpetuates the tradition with the same rigor.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Don Alejandro\", \"color\": \"#3D2008\", \"story\": \"The most ambitious Gran Corona (55×180mm) in the range — 90 minutes of evolution through wood, spice, leather, and chocolate. Production of a few thousand units per year. Score 96 Cigar Aficionado. The primary reason collectors pay attention to the brand.\"}, {\"name\": \"Únicos\", \"color\": \"#4A2810\", \"story\": \"Irregular Perfecto format (54×182mm) that established the brand\'s reputation at its launch. Complex, difficult to roll, almost impossible to find outside Cuba. Notes of aged leather, forest floor, intense dark chocolate.\"}, {\"name\": \"Familiar\", \"color\": \"#5C3317\", \"story\": \"Short Robusto (48×122mm) — the most accessible in the range. All the Robaina signature (oscuro wrapper, deep earthy notes) in a 40-minute format. The recommended entry point into the Robaina universe.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Alejandro Robaina\", \"anecdote\": \"Don Alejandro answered all questions about his cultivation secrets with the same formula: \'The tobacco knows what it needs to do. My job is not to prevent it.\' He never owned a mobile phone and spent his mornings in his plantations until age 90.\"}, {\"name\": \"Hiroshi Robaina\", \"anecdote\": \"Don Alejandro\'s grandson perpetuates the family tradition with identical rigor. He has refused all expansion offers that would have required purchasing tobacco from outside the family\'s San Luis lands.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 25 Años\", \"notes\": \"The definitive terroir pairing — tobacco and sugarcane cultivated kilometers apart. The vanilla sweetness of aged rum against the deep earth of Robaina creates a uniquely insular dialogue.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Cuban coffee sin azúcar\", \"notes\": \"The authentic pairing of Vuelta Abajo growers. Strong unsweetened Cuban coffee amplifies the dark chocolate and forest notes without any interference.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Vegas Robaina';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Jean Villiger founded his cigar workshop in Pfeffikon, in the canton of Lucerne, in 1888. Switzerland is not a tobacco-producing country — but its geographic position at the heart of Europe, its commercial networks, and its tradition of precision craftsmanship made Pfeffikon a logical location for a premium manufacture oriented toward export.\r\n\r\nVilliger\'s originality in the European cigar industry lies in rare versatility: the house masters both small-format production (cigarillos) and large premium formats, covering a spectrum from accessible mass-market to high-end collectibles. This extended range results from a patient acquisition strategy — Villiger has absorbed several European manufacturers over the decades, integrating their expertise and brands.\r\n\r\nThe Premium range is the reason serious collectors take notice of Villiger. Using Brazilian, Ecuadorian, and Indonesian tobacco in blends personally supervised by Heinrich Villiger (fourth generation) until his retirement in 2020, the Premium cigars embody a Swiss approach to cigariculture: precision, consistency, discreet elegance.\r\n\r\nThe Export — the brown cigarillo with its distinctive coffee aroma — is probably the best-selling Swiss cigar in history. Its tubular form, recognizable red band, and accessible price made it the introduction to premium tobacco for millions of European smokers since 1946. It is not Villiger\'s most ambitious product — it is the one that funded everything else and built the brand over two generations.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Villiger Premium No. 6\", \"color\": \"#6B3410\", \"story\": \"Corona format (44×143mm), Brazil/Ecuador/Indonesia blend. The flagship premium proposition — notes of cedar, coffee, soft spices. Built with the precision that German and Swiss markets demand. Consistent score 88-91.\"}, {\"name\": \"Villiger La Meridiana\", \"color\": \"#2C1A0E\", \"story\": \"The exceptional range — tribute to the Italian-speaking Swiss region (Ticino). Ecuadorian Oscuro wrapper on Nicaragua/Brazil blend. More intense profile, dark chocolate and long pepper. Switzerland\'s answer to what the continent can offer against the great New World cigars.\"}, {\"name\": \"Villiger Cuellar Nicaragua\", \"color\": \"#5C3317\", \"story\": \"Collaboration with the Cuellar family in Estelí. Natural Colorado wrapper on a pure Nicaraguan blend. The Swiss positioning in the New World — precise, consistent, less adventurous than Padrón but highly reliable.\"}, {\"name\": \"Villiger Export\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"The legendary cigarillo — tubular, coffee aroma, unchanged since 1946. Smoked in cafés across Central Europe for more than 75 years. A European cultural icon more than a premium cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Heinrich Villiger\", \"anecdote\": \"Fourth generation at the helm of the family house, Heinrich Villiger personally supervised premium blends past the age of 80. He received the Order of Merit of the Federal Republic of Germany for his contribution to European tobacco craftsmanship.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Islay Single Malt\", \"notes\": \"The peat of Islay against the cedar and coffee of the Premium No.6 creates a smoke-on-smoke pairing of great coherence. Laphroaig 10 is the historical reference for this pairing in Swiss smoking rooms.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Espresso Ristretto\", \"notes\": \"For the Export, the founding pairing of the Villiger experience in Central European cafés. Two concentrated expressions — tobacco and caffeine — that mutually reinforce each other.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Villiger';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The name Zino is inseparable from a human figure: Zino Davidoff himself, born in Kiev in 1906, died in Geneva in 1994. When the Davidoff Group decided to resurrect his first name as a standalone brand in 2002, it bet on the symbolic force of a name that had defined European tobacco luxury for half a century.\r\n\r\nThe first incarnation of Zino had been distinct: in the 1980s, Zino Davidoff created under his first name a niche range of cigars, manufactured in Honduras, available only at a handful of carefully selected addresses worldwide. These original Zinos had a reputation for artisanal excellence reserved for insiders. Upon Zino Davidoff\'s death, the range was gradually absorbed into the parent Davidoff brand.\r\n\r\nThe relaunch under the name Zino Platinum in 2002 sought to capture this niche heritage. Positioned deliberately higher than standard Davidoff and more accessibly than limited editions, Zino Platinum occupies a space between the Swiss sophistication of Davidoff and the ultra-premium luxury of rare collections.\r\n\r\nThe Honduran range — using tobaccos from the Jamastran valley — develops a distinctly non-Nicaraguan profile: more floral, more herbaceous, with a volcanic minerality that Davidoff enthusiasts recognize as familial. This is Zino Platinum\'s implicit promise: Davidoff DNA in a darker, more direct Honduran garment.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Zino Platinum Crown\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship range — Honduran Corona with natural Corojo wrapper. Floral and herbaceous, developing white wood, light coffee, and soft spices over 50 minutes. The bridge between Davidoff elegance and Honduran intensity.\"}, {\"name\": \"Zino Platinum Scepter\", \"color\": \"#5C3317\", \"story\": \"The more powerful proposition — Honduran Oscuro wrapper on Jamastran blend enriched with Nicaraguan. Earthy and spiced notes, more assertive structure. For Davidoff enthusiasts seeking an additional power level.\"}, {\"name\": \"Zino Platinum Z-Class\", \"color\": \"#2C1A0E\", \"story\": \"The high-end line — first-choice Honduras Corojo, very limited production. Aged cedar, dark chocolate, complex spices. Price justified by the exceptionality of the leaf selection.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Zino Davidoff (legacy)\", \"anecdote\": \"The brand bears the first name of a man who embodied, in his own words, \'the pleasure of taking one\'s time\'. Zino Davidoff refused to smoke quickly, declaring that \'the cigar is an invitation to slow down — anyone who smokes it in haste has not yet understood what a cigar is\'.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Armagnac 25 Years\", \"notes\": \"Gascon Armagnac, more rustic than Cognac, pairs naturally with the Honduran volcanic minerality of the Zino Platinum. A pairing between two terroir products sharing the same refusal of calculated sophistication.\"}, {\"type\": \"Wine\", \"name\": \"Alsace Grand Cru Riesling\", \"notes\": \"For the Crown range, the petrol minerality and floral sweetness of an Alsatian Riesling amplify the herbaceous and floral notes of the Honduran Corojo wrapper.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Zino Platinum';

-- ── lounges ───────────────────────────────────────────
UPDATE `lounges` SET `description_en` = 'Opened le 6 janv. 2025 par les frères Kamal and Charan Daswani. 160 sqm, walk-in humidor 120 sqm (450+ refs Habanos), smoking lounge lounge 120 sqm (150 people). Open 10h-2h. Group present since 1980, opened par Zino Davidoff en person.', `description_es` = 'Inaugurado le 6 janv. 2025 par les frères Kamal y Charan Daswani. 160 m², walk-in humidor 120 m² (450+ refs Habanos), salón de fumadores lounge 120 m² (150 personas). Abierto 10h-2h. Groupe présent desde 1980, inaugurado par Zino Davidoff en personne.', `description_de` = 'Eröffnund le 6 janv. 2025 par les frères Kamal und Charan Daswani. 160 m², walk-in Humidor 120 m² (450+ refs Habanos), Raucherlounge lounge 120 m² (150 Personen). Geöffnund 10h-2h. Groupe présent seit 1980, eröffnund par Zino Davidoff en personne.', `description_zh` = '2025年1月6日开业 由卡迈勒和查兰·达斯瓦尼兄弟. 160 ㎡, 步入式恒温恒湿雪茄柜 120 ㎡ (450多款哈瓦那斯雪茄), 雪茄休息室 120 ㎡ (150 人). 营业时间10:00-02:00. 集团自1980年起运营,  par Zino Davidoff en 人.', `description_ar` = 'افتُتح في 6 يناير 2025 على يد الأخوين كامال وتشاران داسواني. 160 م², غرفة الهيوميدور للدخول 120 م² (أكثر من 450 سيجارة هابانوس), صالة تدخين السيجار 120 م² (150 شخصًا). مفتوح من 10 صباحًا حتى 2 فجرًا. المجموعة موجودة منذ 1980,  par Zino Davidoff en شخص.' WHERE `id` = '1';
UPDATE `lounges` SET `description_en` = 'Openede in Dec. 2020. All brands Habanos, Arturo Fuente, Davidoff, Rocky Patel, La Flor Dominicana, Plasencia, Gurkha. Accessoires Elie Bleu, Chacom, Zippo.', `description_es` = 'Inauguradoe en déc. 2020. Todas las marcas Habanos, Arturo Fuente, Davidoff, Rocky Patel, La Flor Dominicana, Plasencia, Gurkha. Accessoires Elie Bleu, Chacom, Zippo.', `description_de` = 'Eröffnunde en déc. 2020. Alle Marken Habanos, Arturo Fuente, Davidoff, Rocky Patel, La Flor Dominicana, Plasencia, Gurkha. Accessoires Elie Bleu, Chacom, Zippo.', `description_zh` = '2020年12月开业. 全系列哈瓦那斯品牌, Arturo Fuente, Davidoff, Rocky Patel, La Flor Dominicana, Plasencia, Gurkha. 配件 Elie Bleu, Chacom, Zippo.', `description_ar` = 'افتُتحت في ديسمبر 2020. جميع ماركات هابانوس, Arturo Fuente, Davidoff, Rocky Patel, La Flor Dominicana, Plasencia, Gurkha. إكسسوارات Elie Bleu, Chacom, Zippo.' WHERE `id` = '2';
